# Output the picklist dependency demo harness writes. The harness generates a throwaway
# Salesforce DX project (sfdx-project.json, scratch definition, sample metadata, copied
# framework classes, generated contract classes) so this repository never needs to be one.
# -Step Scaffold rewrites all of it deterministically, so none of it needs tracking — and a
# stray "git add -A" must never commit demo-only Apex or a demo object. That is not
# hypothetical: b6038c1 committed an "undefined/" capture directory exactly this way.
#
# ANCHORED to the repository root. Unanchored, "treecipe/" also matched "src/treecipe/" -- the
# extension's own source tree -- so every new file added under it was silently ignored and a
# "git add -A" staged nothing. The generated output this rule exists for is always written at the
# workspace root, so anchoring loses none of its intent.
/treecipe/
scripts/picklist-dependency-demo/demoSalesforceProject/
